Subject: [PATCH] ARM: OMAP2+: skip unused legacy voltage init on AM335x

AM335x does not populate the legacy OMAP voltage-domain list. Its regulator
and OPP drivers handle voltage control independently of this initialization.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [AM335x board-specific integration]

--- a/arch/arm/mach-omap2/pm.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-omap2/pm.c
@@ -145,7 +145,9 @@
 	omap3_twl_init();
 	omap4_twl_init();
 	omap4_cpcap_init();
-	omap_voltage_late_init();
+	/* AM335x uses regulator/OPP control, not legacy OMAP voltage domains. */
+	if (!soc_is_am33xx())
+		omap_voltage_late_init();
 
 	/* Smartreflex device init */
 	omap_devinit_smartreflex();
